{{also|Gack|gäck}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|găk}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡæk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-gak.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æk}}
* {{homophones|en|gac}}

===Etymology 1===
Apparently {{onomatopoeic|en|nocap=1}} and believed to have first appeared in comic strips. Compare {{m|en|gag|gloss=to choke; to retch}} and {{m|en|hack|gloss=to cough noisily}}.

The "cocaine" and "meth" senses apparently comes from the fact that snorting the drugs often activates a person's gag reflex.

