===Etymology 2===
Apparently {{onomatopoeic|en|nocap=1}}.  Compare {{m+|de|gack|t=call of a hen}}, {{m+|de|gackern|t=(of a chicken) to loudly and repetitive cry}}, and {{m+|nl|gakken|t=(of a goose) to honk}}. 
{{rel-top|Comparison to more terms}}
Pokorny compared {{m+|de|gackern}} to words including {{m+|en|gaggle}}, {{m+|lv|gâgát|t=cry like a goose}}, {{m+|ru|gogotátь|t=(of geese) cackle; laugh loudly}}, {{m+|non|gaga|t=mock, ridicule}}, and {{m+|sq|gogësij|gogësínj|t=yawn, burp}}, among others.<ref name="IEW">{{R:ine:IEW|head=gha gha, ghe ghe, ghi ghi|page=407}}</ref> Pokorny considered common origin or separate innovation both as possibilities to explain the similarities.<ref name="IEW"/>
{{rel-bottom}}

